    95	"I read it for the first time in the week before I came up your bluff, on a road, by the candles of four inns, and for the last time on the morning when I left a seal in a tray. Between those two mornings I read it oftener than I have read anything that I did not write myself. I should like you to hear what was in it, since you have only ever seen it upside down."
    96	
    97	"I've seen most of it."
    98	
    99	"You have seen the sheets. I am speaking of what it was."
