   101	"It began with a day, and a word in square brackets, and after those two lines it was instruments: a registrar at a market town, with a counter and a pen; wardens, who came and stood in a yard and wrote; a panel; the frames of a house on a hill, at the end of every term, and the officers who watched the frames. Each of them laid upon you whatever he had been issued, and wrote down what it showed him, and what it showed him went under the last sheet and was sent up." The left hand moved on the stick. "There was not a paper in that folder which was not somebody's reading of you. I have handled a great many files, and I had not before met one in which the subject had been asked nothing and measured so often."
