   107	Cael did not answer. He had sat across a counter at fourteen while a woman with a pen made a small mark beside a line, and he had learned his letters over again that year, the wrong way up, so that he should know what was being said of him.
   108	
   109	"When the folder had grown as thick as my hand," said Vastin, "the seat did what it does when its instruments have not served. It sent the one that it keeps for such cases. It sent me. I came up that road with a plate, and a set of questions, and three days."
