+   - After: `A cord is made to be run out along a road, and it tells a person how far he may go.`
+   - Ruling: sound. The metaphor develops in one direction and italics add no required vocal distinction.
+
+5. `manuscript/chapter-23.md`, protected chapter-end exchange
+   - Before: `The blanket hung over the gable, with a faint paleness round its edges that did not flicker; and Cael lay back, with the book shut on his chest and his eyes on the slates a yard above him.`
+   - Unit: `"Last time we walked into a place like this," Cael said, "it took four years and a hearing to walk out."` through `"A name and a reason," Karis said. "Older than the walls, under our feet, and nobody's read it because nobody's had a reason to look and a person who could read it in the same lifetime."`
